\section{Imports}

We split imports into two groups: standard library and the learnlog
package.

The commit querying functions ([[get_commits]], [[parse_run_summary]],
etc.) live in the [[commits]] module (\cref{commits}).
The ProgSnap2 exporter lives in [[progsnap2]] (\cref{progsnap2}).
The interactive viewer lives in [[viewer]] (\cref{viewer}).

Four names are imported from inside learnlog rather than restated
here, because the CLI has to apply exactly the rules the runtime
applies.  [[_is_home_or_above]] is the bound that keeps
repository discovery out of the home directory (\cref{learnlog});
[[init]] and [[doctor]] apply it to the roots they are asked to
\emph{create}, where discovery never gets a say
(\cref{sec:setup-home-guard}).  The three names from
[[learnlog._autostart]] are what an interpreter itself consults at
startup to decide whether, and where, to log; [[doctor]] asks them
the same questions and reports the answers
(\cref{sec:autostart-diagnosis}).

