scratch directory under [[tmp_path]] so the test does not
depend on a real venv, and then check: both files exist
with the expected content; a second call with the same
arguments is a no-op (file mtimes unchanged); that a call
which does change a file replaces it rather than emptying
it first; and that an [[OSError]] from [[venv_purelib]]
surfaces as a stderr warning rather than a crash.

Watching the rename is how the last of those stays a test
of the code instead of a test of the machine's timing.  At
the moment the new marker is moved into place the name must
still hold the old project's path in full---which cannot
happen if anything truncated it on the way.

