When both machines have changed the same file the merge cannot
succeed, and the property to check is that failing costs nothing: the
student's file, the local branch, and [[.learnlog/]] are all as they
were, and the message says the word the student needs to search for:

<<test functions>>=
def test_pull_conflict_changes_nothing(workdir, monkeypatch):
    """A conflicting pull aborts without touching anything."""
    from learnlog.cli import app
    from typer.testing import CliRunner
    repo = LearnlogRepo(workdir)
    runner = CliRunner()
    target = _two_machine_log(workdir, runner, monkeypatch)
    student = target / "hello.py"
    student.write_text('print("mine")\n')
    cloned = LearnlogRepo(target)
    monkeypatch.chdir(target)
