\subsection{The [[play]] command}
\label{sec:play}

The most common use of [[play]] is jumping to a tagged
session: [[learnlog play lab1]] starts playback from the
commit tagged [[lab1]].
Therefore the optional positional argument is a Git ref
(tag name, branch, or commit hash), not the source
directory.
The source---a directory containing [[.learnlog/]], a
bundle file, or a ProgSnap2 zip---is specified with
[[--from]] / [[-f]] when needed; it defaults to the
current directory.

The [[-b]] / [[--batch]] flag selects batch mode
(\cref{sec:play-batch}), which prints all commits to standard
output instead of launching the curses viewer.
When the flag is not given explicitly, we auto-detect: if
standard output is not a terminal (for example when piped to
[[less]]), batch mode activates automatically.
This means [[learnlog play | less]] just works without the user
having to remember the flag.

What playback shows by default is the student's own history: their
program runs, and the [[play]] and [[list]] runs in which they read
it back (\cref{sec:filter-learnlog}).
What it leaves out is learnlog's plumbing---the [[pip]] install that
[[learnlog init]] performs, and whatever an older version recorded of
the administrative subcommands that no longer log themselves at all
(\cref{sec:veto}).
The [[--all]] / [[-a]] flag disables that filter.
It is a debugging and archaeology switch rather than a reading one:
the material it restores is setup noise and history from a policy that
no longer applies, which is exactly why the default hides it.

<<typer commands>>=
@app.command()
def play(
    start: Annotated[
        str | None,
        typer.Argument(
            help=(
                "Tag, commit hash, or branch to start "
                "playback from."
            ),
        ),
    ] = None,
    source: Annotated[
        str | None,
        typer.Option(
            "--from", "-f",
            help=(
                "Source: directory with .learnlog/, "
                "a ProgSnap2 zip, or a .learnlog bundle "
                "file. Defaults to current directory."
            ),
        ),
    ] = None,
    batch: Annotated[
        bool | None,
        typer.Option(
            "--batch", "-b",
            help=(
                "Print all commits to stdout instead of "
                "the interactive viewer.  Auto-enabled "
                "when stdout is not a terminal."
            ),
        ),
    ] = None,
    show_all: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--all", "-a",
            help=(
                "Include learnlog's internal runs "
                "(e.g. the pip install from "
                "learnlog init)."
            ),
        ),
    ] = False,
):
    """Interactively play back the development log."""
    import shutil

    repo, tmpdir = resolve_source(source)
    try:
        commits = get_commits(repo)
        if not commits:
            raise SystemExit("No commits found.")

        start_index = 0
        if start:
            <<find starting commit index>>

        <<choose playback mode>>
    finally:
        if tmpdir is not None:
            shutil.rmtree(tmpdir, ignore_errors=True)
