\subsection{The [[analyse]] command}

The [[analyse]] command reads a ProgSnap2 dataset and
generates \LaTeX{} output that presents the student's
development process as a sequence of edit--run pairs.

The source is specified with [[--from]]/[[-f]], matching
the [[play]] command's interface.
Two optional positional arguments [[start]] and [[end]]
restrict the analysis to a range of events.
Each takes the form [[Column=Regex]]---for example,
[[X-Tag=lab1]] to match events tagged [[lab1]], or
[[X-CommitHash=abc123]] to match by commit hash.
The regex is matched with [[re.search]], so partial
patterns work without anchoring.

The source can be:
\begin{description}
\item[A [[.progsnap2]] file] Read directly.
\item[A directory or bundle] Convert to ProgSnap2 on
  the fly using [[do_export_progsnap2]], then read.
\item[Nothing] Use the current directory's
  [[.learnlog/]].
\end{description}

The [[--side-by-side]] flag switches from sequential
(top to bottom) to a causal-chain layout.
The initial edit is rendered full width on its own,
then every following pair is shown as two aligned
rows: one pairing the previous run with the next
edit, and one pairing that edit with the run it
produced.
This makes each cause-and-effect step explicit and
visible on a single line.

The [[--standalone]] flag wraps the output in a complete
\LaTeX{} document with preamble.
With [[--title]], the caller overrides the per-subject
[[\section]] heading---useful when the SubjectID is a
hash or [[anonymous]] and the output is destined for a
report where a human-readable title is preferred.

<<typer commands>>=
